[mind-elixir](https://github.com/SSShooter/mind-elixir-core) engine adapter for [rimir/mindmap](../mindmap). Registers as a `module-type: mindmapengine` so any `<$mindmap>` widget can render via mind-elixir.

## Key features

- **Drop-in adapter** — install alongside `rimir/mindmap`, select `MindElixir` as the default engine
- **Tree-native rendering** — radial layout, expand/collapse, focus, drag with mind-elixir's defaults
- **Round-trip safe** — unknown-namespace attrs (`mx:*`, `kn:*`, etc.) survive engine swaps
- **Bundled library** — mind-elixir UMD + CSS shipped inside the plugin; no CDN or build step

## Prerequisites

- `$:/plugins/rimir/mindmap`
- TiddlyWiki 5.3.0+

## Quick start

1. Install both `rimir/mindmap` and this plugin.
2. Set `$:/config/rimir/mindmap/default-engine` to `MindElixir` (or leave empty — it's the only engine).
3. Render any view: `<$mindmap view="MyView"/>`.

## Bundled version

mind-elixir v5.11.0 (MIT-licensed). See `changelog.tid` for upgrades.

## License

MIT for the adapter code. mind-elixir is bundled under its own MIT licence (preserved at the top of `lib/mind-elixir.umd.js`).
